BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Shelfmark) Tj T* () Tj T* (Shelfmark: Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Every summer, children in low-income neighborhoods lose reading ground that their wealthier) Tj T* (peers do not. Decades of education research show that students from lower-income households can) Tj T* (lose roughly two to three months of reading achievement over the summer, while higher-income) Tj T* (students hold steady or gain slightly. Because the loss compounds year after year, by middle) Tj T* (school the gap can amount to years of reading skill. The gap is not a matter of ability. It) Tj T* (reflects access: fewer books at home, fewer enrichment programs nearby, and parents working) Tj T* (long hours who cannot supervise reading.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Existing fixes fall short. Public library summer programs are valuable but are rarely matched) Tj T* (to an individual child's level, so many children pick books that are too hard, get frustrated,) Tj T* (and quit. Large tutoring chains are expensive and located in wealthier suburbs. Free volunteer) Tj T* (programs struggle with tutor turnover and have no way to measure whether a child is improving.) Tj T* (In our pilot neighborhood, we surveyed 120 parents and found that 83 percent wanted summer) Tj T* (reading help for their child, but only 14 percent had found any program they could afford and) Tj T* (reach on foot.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Shelfmark is a neighborhood tutoring center that combines a physical, welcoming space with) Tj T* (reading-level analytics. When a child enrolls, they complete a fifteen-minute adaptive) Tj T* (diagnostic that places them on a fine-grained reading scale. Our matching engine then does two) Tj T* (things. First, it builds a personal shelf of books that sit in the child's productive range:) Tj T* (hard enough to grow, easy enough to enjoy. The engine also weighs the child's stated interests,) Tj T* (so a ten-year-old who loves soccer gets sports stories at the right level. Second, it pairs the) Tj T* (child with a tutor whose track record and teaching style fit the child's particular profile,) Tj T* (such as decoding difficulty versus comprehension difficulty.) Tj T* () Tj T* (After each session, the tutor logs a two-minute check, and the software updates the child's) Tj T* (level and adjusts the shelf. Parents receive a plain-language progress note. Centers are small) Tj T* (rented storefronts near schools and transit lines, staffed by trained local tutors, many of) Tj T* (them community college students and retired teachers. The physical presence matters: it gives) Tj T* (families a trusted place close to home, and it gives children a reason to show up.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (In the United States there are roughly 17 million children ages 8 to 12, and about one in five) Tj T* (lives in a household below the federal poverty line. Our initial target is the subset attending) Tj T* (Title I schools, approximately 3.5 million children nationally. Within our home metro area) Tj T* (alone, 41 Title I elementary and middle schools serve about 19,000 children in our age range.) Tj T* (If we reach 5 percent of them, that is roughly 950 students per summer from one metro area.) Tj T* () Tj T* (School districts are a second buyer. Districts receive federal and state funds earmarked for) Tj T* (summer learning and learning recovery, and they actively seek vendors who can show measured) Tj T* (outcomes. Our third market is other literacy programs, such as libraries and nonprofits, that) Tj T* (want our matching software without running a center. We estimate the combined serviceable) Tj T* (market in our first three metro areas at about 24 million dollars per year.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We earn revenue from three streams. The first is family fees on a sliding scale from 0 to 18) Tj T* (dollars per session, with an average realized fee of 9 dollars. The second is district summer) Tj T* (contracts, priced at 410 dollars per enrolled student for an eight-week program, which covers) Tj T* (tutor pay, books, and software. The third is software licensing at 6 dollars per student seat) Tj T* (per month to outside programs.) Tj ET
endstream
